; apps/word/welcome.wtx - the shipped WELCOME.DOC's source (SPEC.md 65.4).
; One paragraph per line; leading '.'-directives set the paragraph format,
; {b}..{/b}-style spans set character formats, a literal tab is a tab.
; tools/os88doc.py turns this into a native .DOC deterministically.
.c {d}WELCOME TO MICROSOFT WORD{/d}
.c Version 1.1a for os8088

This document is a native Word .DOC file: everything on this page - the {b}bold{/b}, the {i}italics{/i}, the centered heading above - was saved into it and is being rendered back by the same engine you are typing into.

.open {b}What works{/b}
Type anywhere; select with the mouse, or press F8 and extend with the arrow keys. Character formats live on the ribbon, in Format Character, and on the Ctrl keys: {b}bold{/b} (Ctrl-B), {i}italic{/i}, {b}{i}both together{/b}{/i}, {u}underline{/u} (Ctrl-U), {w}word underline{/w} (Ctrl-W), {d}double underline{/d} (Ctrl-D) and {k}small caps{/k} (Ctrl-K). Paragraph formats come from the ruler, the Ctrl keys, or Format Paragraph.
.li 5 .fi -5 This paragraph wears a hanging indent, set with Ctrl-T; the ruler's markers show it, and dragging them moves it.
.c This paragraph is centered (Ctrl-C).
.r This one is flush right (Ctrl-R).
.sp2 .open This one is double spaced (Ctrl-2) and open (Ctrl-O) - draft view renders the extra leading exactly as the shipped product's did.

.open {b}A few keys{/b}
Ctrl-F	Search
F4 / Shift-F4	Repeat the search down / up
F5	Go To a page
Ins	Overtype (the status bar's OVR lamp)
F8	Extend the selection (EXT)
Shift-F12	Save
F12	Save As
Alt-BkSp	Undo

.open This is Word's draft view - the mode the real product shipped for machines exactly like this one: one fixed-pitch face, character formatting synthesized. The menus, ribbon, ruler, status line and dialogs follow the Opus source release preserved by the Computer History Museum.
Save your own documents into the DOCS folder with Save As; File Open reads plain text files too.
